many led the opening leg, followed by Russia, and they pulled further ahead on the second leg, leading Russia by 1:11.2 at the second exchange. But on the third leg German " [:a {:href "/athletes/81197"} "Simone Greiner-Petter-Memm"] " missed six of her 10 targets, and 12 of 16 shots overall, and was forced to ski 900 metres in penalty loops, posting a time of 30:43.1, slowest by any biathlete on the top seven teams. This dropped Germany to third, but over 2½ minutes behind Russia, and the gold medal chase was over. Russia won by almost four minutes, while Germany pulled back some time on the anchor leg to get the silver medal, over a minute ahead of France."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Misses"] [:th {} "Extra Shots"] [:th {} "Shooting 1 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 1 Extra Shots"] [:th {} "Shooting 1"] [:th {} "Shooting 2 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 2 Extra Shots"] [:th {} "Shooting 2"] [:th {} "Exchange"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Russian Federation"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "1-47:19.5"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Lead-Off"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/82536"} "Nadezhda Talanova"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "27:21.1"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "27:21.1 (2)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2nd Leg"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/82416"} "Nataliya Snytina"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "27:25.4"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "–"] [:td